# SpendSense — AI API Keys (documentation)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⚠️  SpendSense no longer bundles any .env file or key material in the APK.
#     This file is documentation only — never commit real keys to Git.
#
# API keys enter the app exclusively through one of these two channels:
#
# 1. --dart-define (development & CI builds):
#      flutter run \
#        --dart-define=GROQ_API_KEY=... \
#        --dart-define=CEREBRAS_API_KEY=... \
#        --dart-define=GEMINI_API_KEY=... \
#        --dart-define=OPENROUTER_API_KEY=...
#
# 2. In-app AI Provider Settings (Settings → AI Provider Settings):
#    Keys are stored in platform-encrypted storage (Android
#    EncryptedSharedPreferences / iOS Keychain) on the user's device and are
#    the recommended way to configure SpendSense as an end user.
#
# A client-embedded API key is ALWAYS extractable from an installed APK by a
# determined attacker — no bundling technique makes it secret. If per-user
# secret storage is not acceptable for your distribution, proxy the AI
# providers behind your own authenticated backend instead.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

GROQ_API_KEY=
CEREBRAS_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
